You probably could have known that you were going to vomit.  The fact
that the tin had negative nutrition (it took you from Hungry to Weak)
actually guarantees this.  That's not exactly obvious, but the "You are
feeling mildly nauseated" message is, and that appears within a couple
of turns of eating.  You should have seen it before you opened the door.
 Knowing that you're about to be stunned and confused, you shouldn't
head for an area where you know there will be a bunch of monsters, like
one of the uncleared empty rooms in Sokoban.

You don't need to rush forward just because you're Hungry and have no
food, because you can just pray for food under normal circumstances.
(Normal circumstances meaning you don't pray often and you're not doing
anything to hurt your luck or alignment.  (Of course you are not in
Gehennom.))  Just make sure to wait until you're Weak before praying.

At this point in the game you should be pretty close to getting a
unicorn horn, which makes all these problems much less severe.  Until
then, they are just one of the somewhat unavoidable dangers of the early
game.

Unidentified tins are kind of a pain anyway.  I would try to avoid them
unless you're in a safe place, have lots of time, and are only Hungry or
not hungry at all, and even in that case I would just be looking for
spinach or the rare intrinsic, not nutritional value.  In your case I'd
consider just praying and ignoring the tins.

